     "text": "```python\ndef edit_distance(s1: str, s2: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the edit distance between two strings using dynamic programming.\n    Edit distance is the minimum number of operations required to convert one string into another.\n    Allowed operations: insertion, deletion, substitution.\n    \"\"\"\n    m = len(s1)\n    n = len(s2)\n    \n    # Create a 2D table to store the edit distances\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n    \n    # Initialize the first row and column with indices\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        dp[0][j] = j\n    \n    # Fill the table\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            if s1[i - 1] == s2[j - 1]:\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = 1 + min(\n                    dp[i - 1][j],    # Deletion\n                    dp[i][j - 1],    # Insertion\n                    dp[i - 1][j - 1] # Substitution\n                )\n    \n    return dp[m][n]\n```",
